# sync_timedb archive janitor contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

`sync_timedb` separates **hot path** (supervisor: discover → ingest → dispatch append) from **cold path** (`ArchiveJanitor` thread: seal → validate → raw delete → `.tar` drop via day-debt micro-batches). Continuous ingest must not depend on idle windows or blocking supervisor maintenance.

## Two-queue model (2026-06)

| Queue | Thread | Owns |
|---|---|---|
| **Ingest** | MainThread + `ingest_pool` / `archive_pool` | Parse → DB → tar append dispatch; handoff requeue; non-blocking `enqueue_day_close` enqueue |
| **Archival** | `ArchiveJanitor` thread | Seal → verify → **batch delete** → tar drop; proactive discover each tick; drain-until-empty debt processing |

**MainThread coordinator:** enqueue archival work (`signal_work_available`, `signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass`, `_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close`) — **never** block on seal/delete/day_close completion.

**Chunk boundaries are ingest-only:** slot finalize, prewarm, ingest imap, archive append dispatch, pending rescan (with handoff exclusion), and non-blocking day_close **submit**. **Forbidden at chunk end:** `run_supervisor_day_raw_removal_delete_pass`, chunk-spinning `_maybe_handle_raw_removal_delete_phase`, `signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass(reason=every_n_chunks|ingest_queue_empty|day_ingest_complete:…)`, and inline `post_finalize_reconcile` (moved to **`_apply_archive_finalize_results`**). Regression: **`test_arch_supervisor_chunk_loop_does_not_call_apply_batch_delete`** in `test_sync_timedb_architecture_contract.py`.

**Ingest-path tar append stays on `archive_pool`** (including decompress-for-append). Janitor does not replace append workers.

See also **`sync-timedb-canonical-startup-archive-scan.mdc`** (startup snapshot, handoff reconcile, rescan exclusion).

